-- pending: SPEC §33 Open (relabelling a port, decision 57 R2c)
-- A computation parameter called both inside its callee's handler and outside it (SPEC §33
-- *Open*): `twice` calls `f` under its own `to_result` and again outside it, where its caller
-- serves the `raise`. The argument performs its `raise` at one static name, its port, which cannot
-- be both; this waits on relabelling the port at one of the calls (decision 57, R2c).
--
-- Once it lands: `inr i32[1]`: the first call's error is `twice`'s, the second's `main`'s; `live 0`.
--
-- now: 11:65: `with to_result` serves `Fail` for a call of the computation parameter `f`, which is called elsewhere outside a handler of `Fail`, where the caller serves it: the effect a computation parameter provides is served at one site of the function, until a port can be relabelled (SPEC §33 *Open*)
include fail
fn twice(f: !(1 => i32 with Fail[i32])) -> i32 with Fail[i32] = with to_result[i32, i32] { f(()) }; f(())
main -> i32 + i32 = with to_result[i32, i32] { twice(!{ u -> raise(1) }) }
